# Rust service core — Node is client only

Pinforge desktop services and tools run in **Rust** (`pinforge-server`). Node modules are **clients**.

## Roles

| Layer | Role | May do | Must not do |
|-------|------|--------|-------------|
| `apps/desktop` renderer (React) | UI | Call `window.api` / IPC | Node APIs, business download/job logic |
| `apps/desktop` main / preload | Thin host + bridge | Window, dialogs, shell, updater; spawn server; forward IPC ↔ JSON-RPC | Re‑implement jobs/download/enhance/providers/remote |
| `pinforge` / `pinforge-worker` (Rust) | CLI client | Request methods on Rust server; installer / scripting entry | Own long‑running service logic |
| `packages/*` (TS) | Shared client helpers / types / UI‑adjacent | Serialize requests, types, fallbacks only when server missing | Grow new permanent service implementations in Node |
| `rust/` (`pinforge-server`) | Background app server | Execute tools/services; emit progress/job events (callbacks) | — |

## Protocol

- Client → server: NDJSON JSON-RPC `{ id, method, params }`
- Server → client callbacks: `{ event, payload }` (e.g. `download.progress`, `job.updated`, `server.ready`)
- Desktop wires events to renderer IPC; CLI prints or handles events

## When adding a feature

1. Add/extend a **Rust** method + event hooks in `rust/crates/*`
2. Call it from Node via `@pinforge/worker` (`getServerClient().request` / event listeners)
3. Keep Electron for shell-only APIs (dialogs, `shell.*`, auto-update)
4. Playwright / one-shot `pinforge-worker` CLI = temporary fallback only — do not build new Node service paths

## Anti-patterns

- New download/job/settings/remote logic in `apps/desktop/src/process` or TS packages as the primary path
- Treating MediaCore / Node HTTP remote as the long-term service layer
- Skipping server events and polling Node-only state for progress
